name issue_204_cross_traffic_join
describe 2000 kbps of non-responsive cross traffic joins a 3 Mbps bottleneck (300 ms queue) at 10 s and leaves at 25 s: the allocation holds between GoogCC updates, so the queue drains and video doesn't freeze for most of the cross traffic (#204)
# The link of yardstick #294 (yardstick_204_cross_2000). libwebrtc (parity-data-pr/pr/294, seeds 1-10):
# video.freeze_total_ms mean 3590, freeze_count 6.9.
# main before the flip, seeds 1-10: 7547 2203 8396 5545 7703 2071 7359 7773 7478 2116 (mean 5819).
# With `control_handler` and `send_rate_stats` on: 1849 1379 1382 5292 2540 1886 8100 1843 1808 846 (mean 2693).
# sm_compare runs 80 seeds here (#408). Both stacks enter the stuck mode of #390 (cuts end above the free 1 Mbps,
# the queue stays full, about 10 freezes) on about 2.5 % of seeds, depending on the RTCP phase at the join: libwebrtc
# 10 of 400 seed-runs over five RTCPSender schedules (#397), ours 3 of 80 on main d02f90f (seeds 5, 74, 75; mean 2.99
# freezes). On 10 seeds one stuck draw moves the mean by about 0.9 freezes and decides the cell, as seed 5 did after #378.
compare_seeds 80
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=40ms queue=300ms
at 10s cross=2000kbps
at 25s cross=0kbps
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 6000
